 "raw_reply": "{\"item\": \"S441-013\", \"clauses\": {\"give\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F05 asks the learner to name the day or month that follows a given value, which addresses the task of giving the units in order. unit_label can print 'day of the week' or 'month of the year', and v repeats a day or month value from reference_name.\"}, \"days_of_the_week\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"With unit_label set to 'day of the week' and v set to one of the day values in the reference_name list, F05 produces a question about the order of the days of the week.\"}, \"months_of_the_year\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F05\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"With unit_label set to 'month of the year' and v set to one of the month values in the reference_name list, F05 produces a question about the order of the months of the year.\"}, \"correct_order\": {\"verdict\": \"PRODUCIBLE\", \"family\": \"F06\", \"template\": \"What {unit_label} comes right before {v}?\", \"reasoning\": \"F06 asks for the unit that precedes a given day or month, which tests the correct order of both sequences. The same domain limitation noted for F05 applies to its unit and v pairing.\"}}, \"failing_families\": [\"F02\", \"F03\", \"F05\", \"F06\"], \"failing_templates\": [\"{term}\", \"The {elapsed_label} is the number of days or weeks that have passed.\", \"What {unit_label} comes right after {v}?\", \"What {unit_label} comes right before {v}?\"], \"overall\": \"FAIL\", \"reasoning\": \"F03 is a hint whose slot is filled from F02, which prints 'how much time has passed'. The result reads ungrammatically for a grade 1 learner, and its concept of days or weeks that have passed is elapsed time, which is outside this lc's clauses and near the NOT_YET_KNOWN term 'elapsed time'. F02 is the source of that phrase and is judged with it. F05 and F06 each draw unit_label from 'day of the week' or 'month of the year' independently of v, which repeats reference_name values covering both days and months, and no value_derivations link the two. So a question can pair the day unit with a month value, or the month unit with a day value, and the resulting question is wrong for the learner. F07 and F08 are judged as answer choices and pass on the packet as shown: F08 members are drawn from the generator's own distractor list, and the packet does not show whether a distractor can equal the keyed answer. F01 and F04 pass as text: 'date chart' is not in NOT_YET_KNOWN, and the packet does not show a chart being printed with the item.\"}",
